--- a shared helper's refusal names the export whose call made the copy
--- mistakes: 2
--- `chat` and `act` both reach llm's helper `_body_of`; the int handed as
--- `act`'s `system` makes a copy of the helpers whose `len` meets an int.
--- Every refusal names `act` at its line: the valid `chat` call, which
--- reaches the helper first, is not blamed (it had been: a copy lowered
--- before its caller's body had no chain on record, and the first export
--- reaching the helper answered). (It had been Magpie's `lookup` and
--- `latest`, until Magpie became a package of its own.)
use llm

m = reach['http://127.0.0.1:1/v1']
talk = ask['hello']
ok = chat[m, talk, system = 'be brief']
log[ok.ok]
bad = act[m, talk, system = 5]
log[bad.ok]
